---
description: Safety guardrails for local machine environment setup
alwaysApply: true
---
- NEVER modify `~/.gitconfig`, `~/.zshrc`, `~/.bashrc`, or `~/.claude/settings.json` without creating a `.bak` backup first.
- NEVER run `sudo` or Windows Admin elevation commands without pausing and asking the user.
- NEVER write API keys or tokens into tracked repository files.
- ALWAYS detect the host OS (`$IsWindows` / `uname -s`) before suggesting or running package manager commands (`winget` vs `brew`).
